      "content": "While Sudafed is often effective for congestion, decongestants in its pills or liquids can raise your blood pressure and may interact negatively with lisinopril. Because of your prescription medication, you should consult your doctor or pharmacist before taking oral decongestants to ensure it is safe for your specific situation. For safer relief, non-oral options like saline sprays, nasal irrigation, or steam inhalation can help clear pressure without disrupting your blood pressure levels. Please do not take Sudafed without first seeking medical advice regarding your hypertension and lisinopril usage.",
