      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, there is still a significant risk because Sudafed (pseudoephedrine) works by constricting blood vessels in the nose, which also narrows vessels elsewhere in your body and raises blood pressure immediately and sharply. You cannot rely on lisinopril to \"kicker in\" fast enough to counteract a conga amplitude rise happening right now, especially since lisinopril acts as an ACE inhibitor to manage long-term pressure rather than treating sudden spikes. Taking the medication without a confirmed blood pressure check first is dangerous and could lead to severe headaches, heart palpitations, or even a hypertensive crisis.",
